ICU 79 updates to Unicode 18 (blog), including new characters and
scripts, emoji, collation & IDNA changes, and corresponding APIs
and implementations.

It also updates to CLDR 49 (blog) locale data with many additions
and corrections.

Line break backwards-iteration performance has been significantly
improved, fixing a long-standing regression.

C++ and Java implementations of the CLDR MessageFormat 2.0
specification have been updated to CLDR 49. Some of the API remains
in technology preview.

ICU 79 and CLDR 49 are major releases, including a new version of
Unicode and major locale data improvements.
